cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this pipeline in your research, please cite both the software
  repository (below) and the associated article (see preferred-citation).
title: >-
  Phytohormones-Fungi: a reproducible phylogenomic pipeline for
  cross-kingdom homolog detection and analysis
authors:
  - family-names: "García-Estrada"
    given-names: "David Alberto"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1169-5329"
    affiliation: >-
      Center for Research in Advanced Materials (CIMAV), Chihuahua, México
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-15"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DavidAlberto/Phytohormones-Fungi"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"  # Pending
url: "https://github.com/DavidAlberto/Phytohormones-Fungi"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible bioinformatics pipeline for identifying, curating, and
  phylogenetically analyzing homologs of phytohormone-associated genes in
  filamentous fungi and across kingdoms. The pipeline integrates a custom
  taxonomically curated protein database, cross-kingdom BLASTp and profile
  HMM searches with complete-domain validation, phylogeny-aware sequence
  alignment, and maximum-likelihood phylogenetic inference with bootstrap
  support.
keywords:
  - phylogenomics
  - bioinformatics
  - fungi
  - phytohormones
  - cytokinin
  - Trichoderma atroviride
  - homolog detection
  - blast
  - iqtree
  - reproducible-research
